>>
>
> As I said, I'm not saying that I agree with it, nor am I saying I think
> it's correct. What I AM saying is that that is how it is, regardless of
> whether it makes sense, regardless of what the definitions of the various
> NU are, and regardless of whether it should be something else.
>
> That said, I do happen to agree with you. That, however, is not my point.
> This is not my opinion, it is the current state of the language. And I am
